[ti:Why Agent Sessions Change the Rules of Inference]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: An agent can use GPU memory while it's waiting for a tool.
[00:00.00]Ava：智能体等待工具返回时，仍可能占用 GPU 显存。
[00:04.22]How can a paused conversation do that?
[00:04.22]对话都暂停了，怎么还会占显存？
[00:07.33]Brian: Its key-value, or KV, cache can stay in memory between model calls.
[00:07.33]Brian：它的键值缓存，也就是 KV 缓存，可以在两次模型调用之间留在显存里。
[00:12.48]With many agents running, those waiting contexts add up.
[00:12.48]很多智能体同时运行时，这些等待中的上下文就会越积越多。
[00:16.78]That's why this matters for serving.
[00:16.78]所以这对推理服务很重要。
[00:19.90]Ava: So the server sees more than a stream of unrelated questions?
[00:19.90]Ava：服务器看到的不只是一串互不相关的问题？
[00:24.74]Brian: Exactly. An agentic session is a chain of model calls and tool calls.
[00:24.74]Brian：没错。一次智能体会话由一连串模型调用和工具调用组成。
[00:29.93]A coding session may start with a huge prompt, then keep adding to that context on every turn.
[00:29.93]一次编程会话可能从很长的提示词开始，之后每一轮都继续扩充上下文。
[00:37.35]Ava: And a single task can start subagents too.
[00:37.35]Ava：而且单个任务也能启动子智能体。
[00:41.25]Brian: Right. Those subagents may run in parallel.
[00:41.25]Brian：对，这些子智能体可能并行运行。
[00:44.53]Meanwhile, the main agent spends much of its time waiting for tools.
[00:44.53]与此同时，主智能体有很多时间都在等工具返回。
[00:49.72]Its cached context may still occupy space.
[00:49.72]它缓存的上下文可能仍在占用显存。
[00:53.27]Ava: What happens at the start of a long session?
[00:53.27]Ava：长会话开始时会发生什么？
[00:56.64]Brian: The model does a prefill: it processes the input prompt and builds the KV cache it can reuse during generation.
[00:56.64]Brian：模型会先做预填充：处理输入提示词，并建立生成时可复用的 KV 缓存。
[01:04.65]If that cache is evicted, a later call may need to process the context again.
[01:04.65]如果缓存被清除，后续调用可能得重新处理上下文。
[01:10.55]Ava: That sounds expensive when the context keeps growing.
[01:10.55]Ava：上下文不断变长的话，代价听起来很高。
[01:14.84]Brian: It is the problem the article focuses on.
[01:14.84]Brian：这正是文章关注的问题。
[01:17.73]The serving system has to keep useful context available across turns while making room for many sessions at once.
[01:17.73]推理服务系统既要跨轮次保留有用的上下文，也要同时为许多会话腾出空间。
[01:26.06]Ava: What does NVIDIA Dynamo add to see the whole session?
[01:26.06]Ava：NVIDIA Dynamo 靠什么识别整个会话？
[01:30.01]Brian: A stable session ID.
[01:30.01]Brian：一个固定的会话 ID。
[01:31.56]Every large language model request in one agent's chain carries the same identifier.
[01:31.56]同一智能体调用链中的每个大语言模型请求都带着这个标识。
[01:38.08]A child session can also carry its parent's ID.
[01:38.08]子会话也可以带上父会话的 ID。
[01:42.07]Ava: So the ID is like a ticket that stays with the agent, even when it leaves to use a tool?
[01:42.07]Ava：所以这个 ID 就像一张随身票据，智能体去调用工具时也不会丢？
[01:48.18]Brian: That's a useful analogy. Dynamo can connect the returning request to earlier turns.
[01:48.18]Brian：这个比喻很贴切。Dynamo 能把返回的请求与之前的轮次关联起来。
[01:54.39]The session information is available to several optimizations, and each one is opt-in.
[01:54.39]多个优化功能都能使用会话信息，而且每项都需单独启用。
[02:01.18]Ava: Does an agent developer have to change their code?
[02:01.18]Ava：智能体开发者需要改代码吗？
[02:04.91]Brian: For Claude Code, Codex, and OpenCode, Dynamo recognizes identity headers they already send.
[02:04.91]Brian：对于 Claude Code、Codex 和 OpenCode，Dynamo 能识别它们已有的身份请求头。
[02:12.47]Other harnesses can use plugins. A custom harness can send one canonical session header.
[02:12.47]其他智能体框架可以用插件。自定义框架则可以发送一个统一的会话请求头。
[02:20.12]Ava: By harness, you mean the software coordinating the model and its tools?
[02:20.12]Ava：你说的框架，是协调模型和工具的软件吗？
[02:25.03]Brian: Yes. Dynamo maps those different headers into the same internal session information.
[02:25.03]Brian：对。Dynamo 会把不同的请求头映射成相同格式的内部会话信息。
[02:30.94]Downstream components don't need to know which harness sent the request.
[02:30.94]下游组件不必知道请求来自哪个智能体框架。
[02:36.35]Ava: All right. Once requests are connected, what can engineers measure?
[02:36.35]Ava：明白了。请求关联起来后，工程师能测量什么？
[02:42.39]Brian: They can collect session-linked traces.
[02:42.39]Brian：他们可以收集按会话关联的追踪记录。
[02:45.06]Each request gets a record after its response stream ends, with timing, output token count, finish reason, KV cache metrics, and tool-call names.
[02:45.06]每个请求的响应流结束后，都会生成一条记录，包含耗时、输出 token 数、结束原因、KV 缓存指标和工具调用名称。
[02:55.36]Ava: Does that record include the user's prompt?
[02:55.36]Ava：记录里会有用户的提示词吗？
[02:58.61]Brian: By default, it doesn't store prompt, response, or tool-call content.
[02:58.61]Brian：默认不会存储提示词、响应或工具调用的内容。
[03:03.87]Those can be enabled separately.
[03:03.87]这些内容可以分别启用存储。
[03:06.34]The default replay information includes input length and hashes of sequence blocks.
[03:06.34]默认用于重放的信息包括输入长度和序列块的哈希值。
[03:13.10]Ava: Hashes of blocks? What are they for?
[03:13.10]Ava：块的哈希值有什么用？
[03:16.35]Brian: They let replay preserve which prompt prefixes are shared across turns and sessions.
[03:16.35]Brian：它们能让重放保留不同轮次和会话之间共享的提示词前缀关系。
[03:22.43]Think of matching fingerprints.
[03:22.43]可以把它们想成能相互匹配的指纹。
[03:24.67]The replay can recognize a repeated piece of context without using its original tokens.
[03:24.67]重放时无需原始 token，也能识别重复的上下文片段。
[03:31.32]Ava: Wait, so one captured session can become a repeatable workload?
[03:31.32]Ava：等等，也就是说，捕获一次会话就能得到可重复运行的工作负载？
[03:37.00]Brian: Yes. The capture records the requests the agent sent.
[03:37.00]Brian：对。捕获过程会记录智能体发出的请求。
[03:40.68]Engineers can replay that schedule without asking the original agent to make its decisions again or calling its tools again.
[03:40.68]工程师可以按记录的顺序重放这些请求，无需让原智能体重新做决策或再次调用工具。
[03:49.64]Ava: And there are two ways to replay it?
[03:49.64]Ava：重放有两种方式？
[03:52.24]Brian: Offline, AISimulate runs the request graph through a simulated scheduler, router, and KV cache.
[03:52.24]Brian：离线方式是用 AISimulate，让请求图经过模拟的调度器、路由器和 KV 缓存。
[03:59.23]That lets engineers compare policies or cache sizes without spending GPU time.
[03:59.23]这样工程师不用占用 GPU 时间，就能比较不同策略或缓存大小。
[04:05.31]Ava: What about the second way?
[04:05.31]Ava：另一种方式呢？
[04:07.41]Brian: AIPerf replays the same graph against a real Dynamo endpoint on real GPUs.
[04:07.41]Brian：AIPerf 会在真实 GPU 上，向真实的 Dynamo 服务端点重放同一个请求图。
[04:13.02]That's where they measure actual latency, throughput, and cache behavior.
[04:13.02]他们在那里测量实际延迟、吞吐量和缓存表现。
[04:18.90]Ava: So the trace connects agent behavior to what the inference stack did.
[04:18.90]Ava：所以追踪记录能把智能体的行为和推理系统的运行情况对应起来。
[04:23.57]What's the routing problem?
[04:23.57]路由有什么问题？
[04:25.75]Brian: A request-level router places one request at a time.
[04:25.75]Brian：请求级路由器每次只分配一个请求。
[04:29.44]It asks which worker has the best cache overlap with this prompt.
[04:29.44]它会判断哪个工作节点的缓存与当前提示词重合最多。
[04:34.06]That's useful, but it can't see the whole agent's growing working set.
[04:34.06]这有用，但它看不到整个智能体不断扩大的工作集。
[04:39.38]Ava: Working set means the context the session may need again?
[04:39.38]Ava：工作集是指会话之后可能还要用到的上下文？
[04:43.42]Brian: Here, yes: the cached tokens assigned to active programs.
[04:43.42]Brian：在这里是的，指分配给活跃程序的已缓存 token。
[04:48.08]If many agents reach the same step, their combined working sets can exceed GPU memory, then CPU memory.
[04:48.08]如果很多智能体走到同一步，它们的工作集加起来可能先超过 GPU 显存，再超过 CPU 内存。
[04:56.85]Ava: And then the server throws away context it'll soon need.
[04:56.85]Ava：然后服务器就会丢掉很快还要用的上下文。
[05:00.90]Brian: Exactly. It evicts cache from live sessions and later does repeated prefill.
[05:00.90]Brian：没错。它会清除活跃会话的缓存，之后又得重复做预填充。
[05:06.63]The article calls that cache thrashing. The extra work can cut throughput.
[05:06.63]文章称之为缓存抖动。额外的计算会降低吞吐量。
[05:12.55]Ava: Could the router slow agents down before that happens?
[05:12.55]Ava：路由器能在那之前让智能体放慢速度吗？
[05:16.62]Brian: That's the idea behind session-aware admission control.
[05:16.62]Brian：这就是会话感知准入控制的思路。
[05:20.47]Admission control decides when a program can proceed.
[05:20.47]准入控制决定程序何时可以继续运行。
[05:24.18]Dynamo's strategy can apply backpressure when an agent reaches a tool boundary.
[05:24.18]Dynamo 的策略可以在智能体到达工具调用边界时施加背压。
[05:30.05]Ava: Why choose the tool boundary?
[05:30.05]Ava：为什么选工具调用边界？
[05:32.54]Brian: The current model turn can finish.
[05:32.54]Brian：当前这轮模型生成可以先完成。
[05:34.92]Then the program can be paused logically before its next turn.
[05:34.92]然后在下一轮开始前，逻辑上暂停这个程序。
[05:39.27]There's no need to interrupt generation halfway through.
[05:39.27]这样不用在生成到一半时中断。
[05:43.54]Ava: Let's make that concrete. What does the scheduler track?
[05:43.54]Ava：说具体点，调度器会跟踪什么？
[05:47.71]Brian: It groups requests by session ID.
[05:47.71]Brian：它按会话 ID 对请求分组。
[05:50.50]Each program has two states: REASONING or ACTING, and ACTIVE or PAUSED.
[05:50.50]每个程序有两组状态：REASONING 或 ACTING，以及 ACTIVE 或 PAUSED。
[05:56.52]It enters ACTING at a tool boundary.
[05:56.52]程序到达工具调用边界时进入 ACTING 状态。
[05:59.92]Ava: What triggers a pause?
[05:59.92]Ava：什么情况会触发暂停？
[06:02.11]Brian: The scheduler estimates each worker's KV utilization from its assigned programs' token weights and the worker's cache capacity.
[06:02.11]Brian：调度器根据分配给各工作节点的程序的 token 权重，以及节点的缓存容量，估算各节点的 KV 缓存使用率。
[06:10.56]At ninety-five percent, it pauses the smallest ACTING programs until utilization falls to eighty percent.
[06:10.56]达到 95% 时，它会从最小的 ACTING 程序开始暂停，直到使用率降至 80%。
[06:17.90]Ava: Does it resume them as soon as utilization drops a little?
[06:17.90]Ava：使用率稍微下降，就会恢复这些程序吗？
[06:22.25]Brian: It waits until utilization reaches eighty-five percent or less.
[06:22.25]Brian：要等使用率降到 85% 或以下。
[06:26.79]That gap keeps pause and resume from flipping back and forth near the limit.
[06:26.79]这个区间可以避免在阈值附近反复暂停和恢复。
[06:32.61]Ava: And if there's no ACTING program to pause?
[06:32.61]Ava：如果没有 ACTING 程序可暂停呢？
[06:36.56]Brian: It marks the smallest REASONING program for a pause at its next tool boundary.
[06:36.56]Brian：它会标记最小的 REASONING 程序，等它到达下一个工具调用边界时暂停。
[06:41.88]When there's room again, paused programs are considered from smallest token count upward.
[06:41.88]空间腾出来后，会按 token 数从少到多考虑恢复已暂停的程序。
[06:48.29]Ava: Could one small session stay paused forever?
[06:48.29]Ava：小会话会不会一直被暂停？
[06:52.07]Brian: The design includes a thirty-minute forced-resume cap to prevent indefinite starvation.
[06:52.07]Brian：设计中设有 30 分钟的强制恢复上限，避免无限期等待。
[06:58.28]It also briefly boosts the priority of resumed requests.
[06:58.28]恢复后的请求还会短暂获得更高优先级。
[07:02.62]Ava: What did the tests show?
[07:02.62]Ava：测试结果怎么样？
[07:04.58]Brian: In the article's SWE-bench setup, two TP4 MiniMax-M2 replicas ran on one node with eight H100 GPUs.
[07:04.58]Brian：文章的 SWE-bench 测试在一台配备 8 块 H100 GPU 的节点上运行了两个 TP4 MiniMax-M2 副本。
[07:12.01]Program-aware scheduling improved throughput by roughly twelve to sixteen percent over KV-aware routing alone.
[07:12.01]与单独使用 KV 感知路由相比，程序感知调度将吞吐量提高了约 12% 到 16%。
[07:20.62]Ava: So that number belongs to that setup, not every deployment.
[07:20.62]Ava：所以这个数字只适用于那套测试配置，不能套用到所有部署。
[07:25.39]Brian: Right. The article ties the gain to avoiding repeated prefill in that workload.
[07:25.39]Brian：对。文章认为，这项提升来自该工作负载中减少了重复预填充。
[07:30.95]It doesn't claim the same percentage for every model or concurrency level.
[07:30.95]它没有说所有模型或并发水平都能达到同样的增幅。
[07:36.52]Ava: Did they test the idea on agent training workloads too?
[07:36.52]Ava：他们也在智能体训练任务上测试了吗？
[07:40.63]Brian: Yes, on agentic reinforcement learning rollouts.
[07:40.63]Brian：测试了智能体强化学习的轨迹生成。
[07:44.25]At low concurrency, their strategy was roughly even with VERL's default Global LB, or global load balancing.
[07:44.25]低并发时，他们的策略与 VERL 默认的 Global LB（全局负载均衡）表现大致相当。
[07:52.74]Ava: What changed when more agents ran together?
[07:52.74]Ava：更多智能体同时运行时，情况有什么变化？
[07:56.31]Brian: At medium concurrency in that test, model-token throughput was eleven to fourteen point six percent higher.
[07:56.31]Brian：在那项测试的中等并发下，模型 token 吞吐量提高了 11% 到 14.6%。
[08:03.81]At high concurrency, Global LB throughput dropped sharply while the session-aware strategy kept scaling.
[08:03.81]高并发时，Global LB 的吞吐量大幅下降，而会话感知策略仍能继续扩展。
[08:11.44]Ava: That's the scheduling part. What happens when useful KV cache moves out of GPU memory?
[08:11.44]Ava：这是调度部分。如果有用的 KV 缓存从 GPU 显存移出，会怎样？
[08:18.18]Brian: The router needs to know where it went.
[08:18.18]Brian：路由器得知道它被移到了哪里。
[08:21.07]Dynamo already considered cache on a worker's GPU and in its native CPU offload.
[08:21.07]Dynamo 已考虑工作节点 GPU 上的缓存及其原生 CPU 卸载缓存。
[08:26.99]The article adds an experimental index for an external shared store.
[08:26.99]这篇文章又为外部共享存储引入了实验性索引。
[08:32.38]Ava: The shared store here is Mooncake?
[08:32.38]Ava：这里的共享存储是 Mooncake 吗？
[08:35.46]Brian: Yes. Mooncake Store publishes events when objects are stored or removed.
[08:35.46]Brian：对。Mooncake Store 会在对象存入或移除时发布事件。
[08:40.78]Dynamo uses those events to maintain a shared-pool index, so it can account for reusable cache when placing requests.
[08:40.78]Dynamo 利用这些事件维护共享池索引，以便在分配请求时计入可复用缓存。
[08:49.78]Ava: Can it count a page as reusable if only part of that page is in the store?
[08:49.78]Ava：如果存储里只有一个页面的一部分，也能算可复用吗？
[08:55.03]Brian: No. Every physical object needed for the worker's layout must be present.
[08:55.03]Brian：不能。工作节点布局所需的每个物理对象都必须齐全。
[09:00.36]Think of a kit with several parts: one missing part means the kit isn't ready.
[09:00.36]就像一套零件，少一个就没法用。
[09:06.42]Ava: Here's the catch: couldn't the router count the same prefix twice, once on the GPU and once in Mooncake?
[09:06.42]Ava：但有个问题：路由器会不会把同一个前缀算两次，一次算在 GPU 上，一次算在 Mooncake 里？
[09:14.42]Brian: It avoids that. Shared-pool credit applies only beyond the device-resident prefix.
[09:14.42]Brian：不会。共享池只对设备驻留前缀之后的部分计分。
[09:20.64]The placement score then combines native cache overlap, shared-pool credit, and live worker load.
[09:20.64]分配评分会综合原生缓存重叠量、共享池得分和工作节点的实时负载。
[09:28.36]Ava: So far, the router finds cache and controls concurrency. What's next?
[09:28.36]Ava：到目前为止，路由器负责查找缓存和控制并发。接下来呢？
[09:34.90]Brian: The article looks toward programmatic KV cache management.
[09:34.90]Brian：文章接着谈到可编程的 KV 缓存管理。
[09:39.36]Dynamo knows session lifecycles across workers.
[09:39.36]Dynamo 了解跨工作节点的会话生命周期。
[09:42.98]An inference engine such as vLLM or SGLang knows the exact cache state it holds.
[09:42.98]而 vLLM 或 SGLang 这样的推理引擎，清楚自己持有的缓存具体是什么状态。
[09:49.48]Ava: How do those two views work together?
[09:49.48]Ava：这两种视角怎么配合？
[09:52.57]Brian: Dynamo would send a soft KvHint expressing what it wants.
[09:52.57]Brian：Dynamo 会发送软性 KvHint，表达它的意图。
[09:57.01]The engine would decide how to carry that out against its actual cache state.
[09:57.01]引擎再根据实际缓存状态决定如何执行。
[10:03.00]It can clip, delay, or ignore a hint.
[10:03.00]它可以缩减、延后或忽略提示。
[10:06.24]Ava: What might a hint ask for?
[10:06.24]Ava：提示可能要求做什么？
[10:08.55]Brian: Share could move a cached prefix between workers.
[10:08.55]Brian：Share 可以在工作节点之间迁移已缓存的前缀。
[10:11.91]Prefetch could bring KV toward faster memory before it's needed.
[10:11.91]Prefetch 可以在需要之前把 KV 提前移到更快的内存。
[10:16.30]Demote could move it toward a colder tier during a long tool call.
[10:16.30]Demote 可以在漫长的工具调用期间把它移到较冷的存储层。
[10:21.17]Ava: Are all those movements working today?
[10:21.17]Ava：这些迁移现在都能用了吗？
[10:24.06]Brian: The article says Share has a working implementation in HiCache.
[10:24.06]Brian：文章说，Share 已在 HiCache 中实现。
[10:28.66]Prefetch and Demote are designed to build on that machinery.
[10:28.66]Prefetch 和 Demote 计划基于同一套机制实现。
[10:33.04]The broader hint interface is still a proposal.
[10:33.04]更完整的提示接口仍处于提案阶段。
[10:36.82]Ava: What tells Dynamo which cached blocks belong to which session?
[10:36.82]Ava：Dynamo 怎么知道哪些缓存块属于哪个会话？
[10:41.35]Brian: Its Session-Prefix Indexer. It's a radix tree, a tree that groups shared prefixes.
[10:41.35]Brian：靠 Session-Prefix Indexer。它是一棵基数树，按共享前缀组织数据。
[10:47.62]Its branches represent sessions or subagent sessions, and it tracks their KV block locations and lineage.
[10:47.62]树的分支代表会话或子智能体会话，并记录其 KV 块的位置和血缘关系。
[10:56.00]Ava: So it can see a shared beginning and the different paths agents take afterward.
[10:56.00]Ava：这样就能看出共同的开头，以及智能体之后走出的不同路径。
[11:01.70]Brian: Exactly. Engine cache events and router prefix hits keep that view updated.
[11:01.70]Brian：没错。引擎缓存事件和路由器的前缀命中会不断更新这份信息。
[11:07.49]Dynamo is experimenting with policies that use it to decide which hints to send.
[11:07.49]Dynamo 正在试验利用这些信息决定发送哪些提示的策略。
[11:14.00]Ava: Give me the three-point recap before my own context gets evicted.
[11:14.00]Ava：趁我的上下文还没被淘汰，来个三点总结吧。
[11:18.89]Brian: First, a stable session ID connects agent turns.
[11:18.89]Brian：第一，稳定的会话 ID 把智能体的多轮交互串起来。
[11:22.57]Second, traces and session-aware scheduling help measure work and reduce cache thrashing.
[11:22.57]第二，追踪数据和感知会话的调度有助于衡量工作量、减少缓存抖动。
[11:29.41]Third, shared-cache indexing and proposed hints aim to keep useful context available across memory tiers.
[11:29.41]第三，共享缓存索引和拟议中的提示机制，旨在让有用的上下文持续留在各级内存中。
[11:37.82]Ava: Thanks for listening. We'll catch you next time.
[11:37.82]Ava：感谢收听，我们下次见。
